<v Speaker 1>Consider the severity of what this framework implies for you personally.

389
00:28:00.950 --> 00:28:05.110
<v Speaker 1>It brings the stakes of these two parallel creations right down to the individual.

390
00:28:05.190 --> 00:28:14.550
<v Speaker 2>In the physical creation, if you deprive a body of the things it structurally needs, if you take away its physical nourishment, the light of the physical sun, the air it breathes, it suffers deeply and dies.

391
00:28:14.550 --> 00:28:17.990
<v Speaker 1>The physical body inevitably perishes when cut off from its source of life.

392
00:28:18.230 --> 00:28:22.550
<v Speaker 2>But, as the author points out, the physical body was destined to die anyway.

393
00:28:23.270 --> 00:28:26.950
<v Speaker 2>The loss, while tragic in the moment, is ultimately bounded by time.

394
00:28:27.190 --> 00:28:38.790
<v Speaker 1>But the reasoning that makes the Imam of the age the ever-present pole of the universe means that the spiritual creation operates on the exact same structural rules, but with eternal consequences.

395
00:28:38.950 --> 00:28:41.190
<v Speaker 2>A soul that is deprived of its true guide.

396
00:28:41.830 --> 00:28:49.670
<v Speaker 2>A soul that feeds on a counterfeit or wanders without the light of the religious stars faces a spiritual ruin that the body never risks.

397
00:28:49.830 --> 00:28:52.710
<v Speaker 1>The physical death is temporary, a mere transition.

398
00:28:53.110 --> 00:28:57.030
<v Speaker 1>The spiritual ruin, the wandering in the dark without the pivot, is lasting.

399
00:28:57.190 --> 00:29:03.350
<v Speaker 2>That is why the search for the genuine center cannot be abandoned and why the physical universe was built to point toward it.

400
00:29:03.430 --> 00:29:09.030
<v Speaker 1>The Imit is the pole and foundation of religion, the office that never lapses while the messenger comes and goes.

401
00:29:09.110 --> 00:29:11.430
<v Speaker 2>And so we are left with the final

402
00:29:11.550 --> 00:29:14.630
<v Speaker 2>unavoidable challenge of the author's architectural reality.

403
00:29:14.950 --> 00:29:27.750
<v Speaker 1>If the universe itself is testifying to a single unyielding center, and if human history is cluttered with elaborate comforting forgeries designed to distract you from it, which counterfeit are you still building your life on?
